-- title:
--   Layerwise smooth-point stalks from the base layer, q=2
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $q = 2$, and $M'$ is a nonzero natural number not divisible by $q$; a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$ is fixed (hypotheses `hℓg`, `hℓg12`, `hℓgM'`). Further data: a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` lying over $q$ in the sense that $q$ is a nonunit of $A$ (`hA`); a finite set $W$ of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa, M')$ over $\kappa =$ `ResidueField A`, whose members are exactly the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`, i.e. the rational affine geometric places whose $j$-value lies in `ssJSet q κ` (`hW`); the inclusion `hle` of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside Laurent series) into $F := \mathrm{fieldBar}\,q\,M'$, the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-base change of the function field of the curve $X_H$ of level $q^2M'$ with $H = \ker((\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times)$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}(\kappa,M')$, together with the hypothesis `hR₀` that every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ lies in $R_0$'s ring of integers and has $R_0$-residue equal, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, to the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a distinguished element $s$ of $W$.
--
--   A base field of constants is fixed: an intermediate field $k_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ and an element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that the valuation subring $A \cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); moreover every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$ (`hκ`).
--
--   Rigidifying auxiliary data: a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \ge 3$, $\ell \neq q$ and $\ell \nmid M'$; an element $\zeta_0 \in k_0$ whose image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity; and an element $\varpi_t \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1} = q\,u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$ (`hϖt`).
--
--   The layers: a type $\iota$, a family $K : \iota \to$ intermediate fields of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/k_0$ with each $K_n$ finite over $k_0$ (`hKfin`), valuation subrings $A_n$ of $K_n$ cut out by $A$, i.e. $x \in A_n \iff x \in A$ (`hAn`); and the base layer: $K_b = \bot$, that is $k_0$ itself (`hKb`), a valuation subring $A_b$ of $K_b$ cut out by $A$ (`hAb`), and a generator $\varpi_b \neq 0$ of the maximal ideal of $A_b$ (`hϖb`, `hϖb0`).
--
--   The conclusion is stated for $F$ regarded as a $k_0$-algebra through $k_0 \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q} \to F$. It asserts: for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ and every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ such that (generation) $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}) \vee F_0 = F$, and (linear disjointness) for every finite extension $K'/k_0$ inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, every $m$, every $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and every $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with all $a_i$ in $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of}\ K') \vee F_0$, $K'$-linear independence of $c$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ force all $a_i = 0$; and for every field $\mathrm{FSS}$ that is a $\kappa$-algebra and every regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ from $F$ to $\mathrm{FSS}$ (a valuation subring $R.\mathrm{integers}$ of $F$ with a surjective residue map onto $\mathrm{FSS}$ whose kernel is the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with the scaling property of `RegularProlongation`) such that (compatibility) for $f \in F_0$ one has $f \in R.\mathrm{integers} \iff f \in W_0$ — the base-layer package implies the all-layers package, as follows.
--
--   Both packages begin with the same Drinfeld identification block: for every $\kappa$-algebra structure on $\kappa$ over $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$, assuming $\mathrm{CoordRing}\,q\,\kappa$ is a domain, and for every $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$), there are a subgroup $C_s$ of the $(q+1)$-st roots of unity of $\mathrm{GaloisField}\,q\,2$ and a $\kappa$-algebra isomorphism $e$ from $\mathrm{FSS}$ onto the fixed field $\mathrm{quotField}\,q\,\kappa\,C_s$ inside the Drinfeld function field, such that $\#C_s$ equals $\mathrm{placeWidthChar}\,q\,M'$ of the place $s$, and such that for every $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ for which $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$ and for which $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma, 1)$ lies in $\mathrm{hSubgroup}\,q$, the automorphism $R.\mathrm{resAut}$ of $\mathrm{FSS}$ induced by $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma^{-1}$ corresponds under $e$ to the action $\mathrm{hFunctionFieldAction}\,q\,\kappa$ of that element.
--
--   The antecedent further asserts the existence of a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_b(Q) \subseteq F$, ring homomorphisms $\varphi_b(Q) : A_b[X] \to S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q) : S_b(Q) \to \kappa$, and sets $D_b(Q)$ of places of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, indexed by places $Q$, with: $\#N = q+1$; an affine-chart clause, namely a subring $B \subseteq F$ contained in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, contained in $S_b(Q)$ for every $Q \notin N$, and such that every $z \in \mathrm{FSS}$ integral at all $Q \notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$; and, for every $Q \notin N$: the image of $A_b$ in $F$ lies in $S_b(Q)$; $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a)$ equals the image of $a$ for $a \in A_b$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(C\,a))$ equals the residue of $a$ in $\kappa$; $\chi_b(Q)(\varphi_b(Q)(X)) = 0$; $S_b(Q)$ is local with $\ker \chi_b(Q)$ its maximal ideal; $S_b(Q)$ is contained in $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of}\ K_b) \vee F_0$ and every element of that field is a quotient $g/h$ with $g, h \in S_b(Q)$, $h \neq 0$; $\varphi_b(Q)$ is formally smooth, formally unramified and essentially of finite type; all elements of $S_b(Q)$ lie in $R.\mathrm{integers}$, and such an element lies in the maximal ideal of $R.\mathrm{integers}$ exactly when it is divisible by $\varphi_b(Q)(C\,\varpi_b)$; for every $f \in S_b(Q)$ the $R$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation ring of $Q$ and its residue there is the image of $\chi_b(Q)(f)$ in the residue field of $Q$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_b(Q)(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; and $D_b(Q)$ consists exactly of those places $P$ of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ which are rational, for which every $f \in S_b(Q)$ is $P$-integral with $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f \in A$, and for which $A$-valuation of $P.\mathrm{evalAt}\,f$ is $< 1$ precisely when $\chi_b(Q)(f) = 0$. Finally the antecedent requires: the discs separate the places, i.e. $P \in D_b(Q) \cap D_b(Q')$ with $Q, Q' \notin N$ forces $Q = Q'$; at every $P \in D_b(Q)$ with $Q \notin N$ the order of the image in $F$ of the $j$-series `jq` (the element of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\,M'$ given by the coefficient embedding of `jq`, included via `hle`) is $\ge 0$; and equivariance: for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the automorphisms $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$ with $\zeta \in \mathrm{Idx}\,q$ and $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$ which preserves $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism leaves $N$ invariant, and for $Q \notin N$ one has $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_b(Q)) = D_b(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau) \cdot Q)$, where $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,D = \{P \mid \tau^{-1}\cdot P \in D\}$.
--
--   The consequent asserts the same Drinfeld identification block together with the existence of a finite set $N$ of places of $\mathrm{FSS}$ over $\kappa$, subrings $S_n(Q, n) \subseteq F$, homomorphisms $\varphi_n(Q,n) : A_n[X] \to S_n(Q,n)$ and $\chi_n(Q,n) : S_n(Q,n) \to \kappa$, and sets $D_n(Q,n)$ of places of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$, indexed now by a place $Q$ and a layer $n \in \iota$, with: $\#N = q+1$; the affine-chart clause, namely a subring $B \subseteq F$ inside $R.\mathrm{integers}$, inside $S_n(Q,n)$ for all $Q \notin N$ and all $n$, and such that every $z \in \mathrm{FSS}$ integral at all $Q \notin N$ is the $R$-residue of some element of $B$; and, for every $Q \notin N$, for every layer $n$: $A_n$ surjects onto $\kappa$ under reduction; the image of $A_n$ in $F$ lies in $S_n(Q,n)$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)$ is formally smooth and formally unramified; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a)$ is the image of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,a))$ is the residue of $a$; $\chi_n(Q,n)(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)) = 0$; for each $c \in A_n$ with residue $0$ there is a unique ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$, compatible with $\chi_n(Q,n)$ after reduction, and sending $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ to $c$; every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ with $R$-residue $Q$-integral, whose residue at $Q$ is the image of $\chi_n(Q,n)(f)$; the $R$-residue of $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ has $Q$-order $1$; $D_n(Q,n)$ is described exactly as $D_b(Q)$ above, with $S_n(Q,n)$ and $\chi_n(Q,n)$ in place of $S_b(Q)$ and $\chi_b(Q)$; $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) \neq \varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,c)$ for all $c \in A_n$; $S_n(Q,n)$ is local with maximal ideal $\{f : \chi_n(Q,n)(f) = 0\}$, Noetherian, and a unique factorisation monoid; $S_n(Q,n)$ is contained in $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of}\ K_n) \vee F_0$, and every element of that field is a quotient of elements of $S_n(Q,n)$ with nonzero denominator; the linear-disjointness clause holds for $K_n$ (for all $m$, all $c : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and all $a : \mathrm{Fin}\,m \to F$ with values in $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of}\ K_n) \vee F_0$, $K_n$-independence of $c$ and $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ force $a = 0$); every ring homomorphism $\chi : S_n(Q,n) \to A_n$ splitting $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$ and compatible with $\chi_n(Q,n)$ has kernel generated by $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X) - \varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\chi(\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)))$; there is a uniformiser $\varpi$ of $A_n$ (nonzero, generating the maximal ideal) such that $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ is prime, such that an element $f$ of $k_0(\mathrm{image\ of}\ K_n) \vee F_0$ lies in $R.\mathrm{integers}$ precisely when $f = g/h$ with $g, h \in S_n(Q,n)$ and $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi) \nmid h$, and such that for every prime $p$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ not associated to $\varphi_n(Q,n)(C\,\varpi)$ and every $x \in S_n(Q,n)$ there is a monic polynomial $r$ over $A_n$ with $p$ dividing the value at $x$ of $r$ pushed forward along $\varphi_n(Q,n) \circ C$; and there is a finite subset $G$ of $S_n(Q,n)$ such that every $f \in S_n(Q,n)$ can be written as $g/h$ with $g$ and $h$ in the subring generated by $G$ together with the image of $A_n$, and $h$ the image of a unit of $S_n(Q,n)$.
--
--   The consequent also asserts a compatibility block across layers: the assignments are monotone, $K_n \le K_{n'}$ implying $S_n(Q,n) \subseteq S_n(Q,n')$, and moreover for $K_n \le K_{n'}$ the ring $S_n(Q,n')$ is contained in the subring generated by $S_n(Q,n)$ together with the image of $A_{n'}$; the elements $\varphi_n(Q,n)(X)$ have one and the same image in $F$ for all $n$; and $\chi_n(Q,n')$ restricts along the inclusion to $\chi_n(Q,n)$ whenever $K_n \le K_{n'}$. Finally, as in the antecedent but for each layer: for $Q, Q' \notin N$ and each $n$, a place $P$ lying in both $D_n(Q,n)$ and $D_n(Q',n)$ forces $Q = Q'$; the order at every $P \in D_n(Q,n)$ of the image of the $j$-series in $F$ is $\ge 0$; and for every $\tau$ in the subgroup generated by the $\mathrm{levelAutBar}\,q\,M'\,\zeta\,\gamma$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_0(M')$, preserving $R.\mathrm{integers}$, the induced residue automorphism leaves $N$ invariant and satisfies $\mathrm{smulDisc}\,\tau\,(D_n(Q,n)) = D_n(R.\mathrm{resAut}(\tau)\cdot Q, n)$ for all $Q \notin N$ and all $n$.
--
--   This is the functorial (base-change) step in the construction of the supersingular column of the special fibre of the full-level modular curve at the prime $q = 2$ over a rigidifying auxiliary level: the smooth-point charts over the base layer $k_0$ are propagated, together with their Drinfeld identification, their affine chart, their residue discs and their $\Gamma_0(M')$-equivariance, to every finite layer $K_n/k_0$, with the transition compatibilities between layers. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_smoothPointPackages_nodePresentations_nodeCharts_hasseJ_drinfeldInertia_of_eq_two_of_dvd_affineChart), which assembles the supersingular data at $q = 2$ into the semistable model.
